Third-party components
----------------------
The U-Net architecture used by the architecture workflows is based on the
open-source ZeroCostDL4Mic 2D multilabel U-Net (Henriques Lab), which is
itself derived from Ronneberger et al. 2015 (U-Net: Convolutional Networks
for Biomedical Image Segmentation). See:
    https://github.com/HenriquesLab/ZeroCostDL4Mic
Original ZeroCostDL4Mic code is distributed under the MIT License.

The data used in the associated analyses are described in the accompanying
paper; please see the paper's Methods and Data Availability statements for
details on the source patient cohort and ethical approvals.
